[{:db/id 17592186347593 :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,2\\le z\\le 3y+x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type I region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2}^{3y+x}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}[z]_{z=2}^{z=3y+x}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}3y+x-2\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+xy-2y]}_{y=1}^{y=4}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,[(24+4x-8)-(\\frac{3}{2}+x-2)]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3x+\\frac{33}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{33}{2}x]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{33}{2}(2)-0 \\\\  & =39.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
